// CotSC Batch 18 - extracted original English dialogue for tormcr_npcs.d
// Keep existing @ numbers stable when translating.
@1 = ~Hold! Who's... you're people! Real people!~
@2 = ~It's okay. Who are you?~
@3 = ~Are you sent by Randalla Brasshorn?~
@4 = ~We are bandits and you're in our way so you better move aside.~
@5 = ~You're Alma's minions! Sent down here to finish me?! You won't take me alive!~
@6 = ~My name is Isaac. Isaac Wildflame. I am a Harper. No need in secrecy now after everything. I've been sent to investigate disappearances in Torm's Hand and ended up trapped here and left as food for the undead.~
@7 = ~You know Randalla?~
@8 = ~This vile woman bewitched us all. I trusted her like a fool. I should've seen the signs.~
@9 = ~Who are you talking about?~
@10 = ~We need to get out of here.~
@11 = ~Have you seen the missing people?~
@12 = ~That witch Alma! Who else! She pretends to be Torm's acolyte and headmistress of the church. In reality, she's a two-faced necromancer working for some Dark Lord. She trapped me here with her 'creations'. Calling me a form of art, twisted witch.~
@13 = ~All exits are blocked with some invisible barrier of her creation. She imprisoned us. As long as she is alive, we are nothing more than mere prey for her 'pets'.~
@14 = ~Have you seen all these zombies and ghouls? THEY are the missing people. She transformed them using dark arts. One can only guess what her endgame is but some Dark Lord is involved in these machinations. She spoke pretty highly of him.~
@15 = ~This caves had way too many undead for a small village the size of Torm's Hand. She must've been collecting commoners from other villages around as well.~
@16 = ~If she's up there and we are stuck down here, there's no way for us to reach her because of the barrier.~
@17 = ~Being stuck here granted me the opportunity to scout this area, indefinitely. South-east of here lies a chamber with Asmodeus symbol in its centre.~
@18 = ~To Asmodeus, animating a corpse is a waste of a good soul. He wants the mortal's soul bound to a strict, inescapable infernal contract so it will automatically descend to the Nine Hells upon death to be forged into a new devil. What Alma does is the opposite. She sucks the life out, transforming her victims into the undead. That doesn't make any sense.~
@19 = ~I'll stay here. I've been fending walking corpses for past few days, I barely have strength to walk. Take a look around the chamber and try to see what you can find. There has got to be a way out of this place.~
@20 = ~Be careful. This place is really dangerous.~
@21 = ~My name is Jaheira. Sarkyn. Our task was to find you and fulfil your quest.~
@22 = ~Ah, Sarkyn. You're one of us. You have no idea how much comfort that brings me. I was imprisoned here for ghouls to feast on my body once they finally get me. With you, I have better chances at surviving in this hellhole.~
@23 = ~Asmodeus is the supreme ruler of all devils and the undisputed master of the Nine Hells. Hungry for power warlocks or necromancer, like Alma, often draw directly from his power or the power of his subordinate archdevils. Maybe she is his worshiper.~
@24 = ~To Asmodeus, animating a corpse is a waste of a good soul. He wants the mortal's soul bound to a strict, inescapable infernal contract so it will automatically descend to the Nine Hells upon death to be forged into a new devil. What Alma does is the opposite. She sucks the life out, transforming her victims into the undead. That doesn't make any sense.~
